{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id398861833"}, "name":{"label":"natasha moron"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-15T11:40:02-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.88.0"}, "id":{"label":"14553651746"}, "title":{"label":"Why you are taking my raw voice for and giving it to Telisha \"Nikki\" Jones. Hello Suno Support,\n\nTha"}, "content":{"label":"NOTE TO SUNO SUPPORT — SPECIFIC SONG REVIEW\n\nHello Suno Support,\n\nMy name is Natasha Moron, and I am contacting you regarding a specific Suno-generated song that I would like to have reviewed.\n\nI understand from your recent response that if I come across a specific Suno-generated song at a Suno.com URL that I believe requires review, I should provide the specific link.\n\nI would like to do that because I want to understand exactly what happened with this particular song and whether any copyright or content-protection system was involved.\n\nThe song I am referring to is:\n\nSuno song URL: __________________________\n\nI am asking for a careful review of this specific song and, if possible, an explanation of:\n\n* What generated the song;\n* Whether any copyright-protection system was triggered;\n* Whether there was an automated match or detection;\n* What material, if any, was identified by the system;\n* Whether the song contains material associated with another work;\n* Whether my own creative material was involved in the detection;\n* Whether the song was altered, restricted, or otherwise affected by an automated system; and\n* Whether there is anything I need to understand about this particular song.\n\nI am not trying to claim another person’s work.\n\nI am simply asking Suno to review the specific song and explain what your system identified.\n\nMy name is Natasha Moron, and my own music, lyrics, creative ideas, and real human voice are important to my identity as an independent singer, songwriter, musician, and creator.\n\nThank you for reviewing this specific song and providing whatever information you can about what occurred.\n\nSincerely,\nNatasha Moron\nIndependent Singer • Songwriter • Musician • Creator\n\nI am choosing peace, patience, and truth.\n\nI know who I am. You don’t let me use my raw real voice on suno\n\nI am Natasha Moron — a real human being, singer, songwriter, artist, and creator. My life is my own. My voice is my own. My words, experiences, ideas, recordings, and creativity are deeply personal to me.\n\nI recognize that Xania Monet is publicly described as an AI-generated music persona created by Telisha “Nikki” Jones, who has spoken publicly about using Suno to create music. I am not here to attack anyone, take away anyone’s success, or make accusations without evidence.\n\nI simply want my own identity and creative work to be respected.\n\nIf questions arise about voices, lyrics, recordings, musical ideas, or other creative material, I believe the right way to address them is through facts and legitimate evidence — original recordings, dated lyrics, drafts, project files, credits, upload histories, and other documentation that can be independently reviewed.\n\nI don’t want Internet arguments.\nI don’t want hatred.\nI don’t want revenge.\nI don’t want anyone’s life.\n\nI want my own life, my own voice, and my own creative journey.\n\nYou have your journey, and I have mine.\n\nI will continue to protect my creativity while also protecting my peace. I will not allow fear, confusion, or other people’s opinions to make me forget who I am.\n\nLet the evidence speak. Let the truth be examined. Let the facts speak louder than assumptions.\n\nI am going to keep singing.\nI am going to keep writing.\nI am going to keep creating.\nI am going to keep believing in my dreams.\n\nSome dreams don’t die because the road becomes difficult.\n\nI believe God has given me the strength to keep moving forward. I don’t have to rush what is meant for me. I can be patient, stay grounded, and allow things to happen naturally.\n\nMy voice is part of my story.\nMy creativity is part of my story.\nMy dreams are part of my story.\nMy life is part of my story.\n\nAnd I will continue telling my story, in my own voice, in my own way.\n\nI am Natasha Moron.\nI am still here.\nI am still creating.\nI am still singing.\nAnd I am still moving forward. ❤️🎶🙏🏽", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6480136315&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
