{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id105353859"}, "name":{"label":"Big mike 60411"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-15T10:48:28-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.88.0"}, "id":{"label":"14553502770"}, "title":{"label":"Turning into a social media site…"}, "content":{"label":"This update completely ruined the Suno app for me.\n\nI pay a premium monthly price because I use Suno as a WORK TOOL. I am creating, remixing, testing versions, comparing generations, and trying to get actual work done. I am not opening Suno because I want a social-media-style discovery feed pushed into my workflow.\n\nBefore this update, I could create a song, generate more versions, and continue working through those generations in a logical, continuous flow. Now Suno gives me the two songs I generated and then immediately fills the rest of the screen with recommended songs from other people.\n\nI have absolutely no interest in that.\n\nI am not there to browse other creators. I am not there to discover music. I am not there to scroll through recommendations. I am there to work on MY OWN MUSIC.\n\nEven worse, when I generate additional versions of my own song, those new generations are no longer presented together in the same clean workflow. I have to open another section just to find the two new songs I just created, while unrelated recommended music is taking up space in the main feed.\n\nHow is that an improvement?\n\nYou took something that felt like a useful creative production workspace and turned it into another social media experience.\n\nIf people want recommendations and discovery, that is perfectly fine. Give them a Discover tab. Give them a toggle. Give them an option.\n\nBut do not force it into the creation workflow of paying subscribers.\n\nI am paying every month to CREATE MUSIC, not to have other people’s music placed in front of me while I am trying to work.\n\nThis update made the app more cluttered, more frustrating, and less useful for serious creation.\n\nPlease give users an option to COMPLETELY DISABLE RECOMMENDED SONGS and restore the continuous generation workflow so all versions of the same creation stay together.\n\nNot every app needs to become social media.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6480136315&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id228798851"}, "name":{"label":"21thougts"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-15T10:10:32-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.88.0"}, "id":{"label":"14553389992"}, "title":{"label":"2000 to 30"}, "content":{"label":"Well here I am again. I’ve had this app since September 2025. And they needed this app a lot. They changed the algorithm because I assume they’ve been sued to kingdom come and now they took away the amount of songs you can make, because they say they’re will be more quality. Really Suno? More quality.  It’s like this app keeps sinking itself deeper and deeper into the mud.  But as what happens with many things that get popular they’re a bait and switch . I cancelled my year subscription. Good going Suno.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6480136315&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1839580062"}, "name":{"label":"AlfonzoCreative"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-15T10:10:08-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.88.0"}, "id":{"label":"14553388746"}, "title":{"label":"Suno V6"}, "content":{"label":"Hello Suno team,\n\nI’ve happily paid for my subscription over the past several months. The previous models allowed me to create music with beautiful melodies, a style I truly enjoyed, and a sound that conveyed genuine emotion.\n\nHowever, now that model 6 is the only option available in my account, my experience has changed. The sound feels overly synthetic to me, and I feel it has lost the warmth, musicality, and melodic sensitivity I valued so much.\n\nPlease consider allowing subscribers to choose the previous models again. Having access to them would be a reason for me to keep my subscription.\n\nUnfortunately, if this new model remains the only option, I’ll have to cancel because I no longer feel I can get the same value from the service. That’s disappointing, because I truly enjoyed creating music with Suno.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I hope you’ll take this feedback into account.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6480136315&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
